@Isaac The Red
someone else previously discussed using the local file system to speed up development iteration, so you're the second person to come up with that assumption. If you use Android Studio to deploy debug builds then it will only push Asset changes, so it's actually faster to not do this and tell you to use the debugging tools like a real Android developer.
OBB support needs some experimentation, I have ideas that will work if the Android platform lets it work, but this needs development time and development time needs money.

